{
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000030.title": "The Water Tank",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000030.quest_desc": [
    "You never fill this one. In the spreader it holds nothing you can put in or take out, and it does not need to see sky. The Tree Nursery uses the same block later and does hold water in it.",
    "",
    "You have made one already; it is inside your Rain Collector. The spreader needs its own.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000031.title": "The Solar Panel",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000031.quest_desc": [
    "Caps the tower.",
    "",
    "It also makes FE in direct daylight, and it keeps making it once it is part of a spreader, so build where that top block sees open sky if you want the power off it. The spreader runs on nothing and does not care either way.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000032.title": "What the Pump Was For",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000032.quest_desc": [
    "Salvage had you pull one out of a washing machine. This is the machine it was for.",
    "",
    "If you need another, that same teardown also teaches an idea toward the Pump. Four of those make the blueprint, and after that you craft them instead of hunting for more washing machines.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000033.title": "The Grass Spreader",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000033.quest_desc": [
    "Put the core down on ground you want green and it pulls the rest of the parts out of your inventory. Carrying none, it waits while you stack them by hand: tank, pump, a copper pipe on each of the pump's four sides, panel on top. Sneak-place for a bare core and no assembly.",
    "",
    "Formed, it turns coarse dirt to grass out to a radius and keeps doing it, consuming nothing. It skips ground that is roofed over or too dark, since grass would die there anyway.",
    "",
    "Break any one part and the whole machine comes apart and hands back every piece.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000034.title": "Mound Ground",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000034.quest_desc": [
    "The dark earth under a mound's footprint. Dark ground means that mound is coming back, regrowing toward the size it was.",
    "",
    "Green it and it is finished. Erosion can take the grass off later without ever putting the dark back.",
    "",
    "So pick your mounds. One that refills is income; a retired one pays you in what the land grows instead.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000035.title": "The Frontier",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000035.quest_desc": [
    "Welcome mentioned this. It starts now.",
    "",
    "Soil bordering the dump reverts, one ring at a time, and only while you are near it. Every kind of dirt goes, grass included, and it makes no difference who put it there. Interior ground keeps until the edge reaches it.",
    "",
    "Coarse dirt is not the only thing that presses. An unquarried mound, a trash bag or a bale leans on the ground beside it the same way.",
    "",
    "Buildings are safe. Soil is the only thing this ever takes.",
    "",
    "Inside the spreader's radius it is a draw, since the machine re-greens what went back. Ground is lost at the rim.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000036.title": "The Compost Heap",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000036.quest_desc": [
    "Organic muck and fiber scrap are the staples, but it takes most plant matter: leaves, saplings, flowers, crops, seeds, mushrooms. Once a layer has finished, right-click it and the compost turns out of the face you clicked.",
    "",
    "Everything after this runs on what comes out of it.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000037.title": "Fertilizer",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000037.quest_desc": [
    "On reclaimed grass it scatters plants across about the patch vanilla bone meal covers, rippling outward from the click. It does nothing on coarse dirt and is not spent there, so grass comes first.",
    "",
    "On mycelium it puts up mushrooms instead, which is the food loop rather than ground work.",
    "",
    "Anywhere else it works as plain bone meal. That matters more than it sounds: nothing here drops bones, so this is the only thing that will hurry a crop or a sapling along.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000038.title": "Cover",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000038.quest_desc": [
    "A plant on the border is stripped instead of the soil under it. You lose the plant and keep the ground.",
    "",
    "So a border you are holding goes bare before it goes brown. That is your warning, and fertilizing it again puts the cover back.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000039.title": "Farmland",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000039.quest_desc": [
    "No hoe exists here and tilling is switched off, so farmland is crafted rather than dug.",
    "",
    "Fertilizer and dirt make it. Coarse dirt works too and costs four times the fertilizer, so it is cheaper to break a patch of your own reclaimed grass for dirt than to convert the dead ground directly.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003A.title": "Keep It Wet",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003A.quest_desc": [
    "Wet farmland is left alone. Dry farmland reverts like any other soil, and the crop standing on it drops on the floor rather than being destroyed, so you lose the plot and the growth but keep the seed.",
    "",
    "Put the plot inside the spreader's radius. It spares moist farmland the same way it re-greens grass, so the machine that made the ground holds the farm too.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003B.title": "The Unknown Seedling",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003B.quest_desc": [
    "Something comes up in a finished compost layer now and then and turns out along with the fertilizer.",
    "",
    "No recipe makes one and nothing in the world drops one. More compost is the only way to more seedlings.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003C.title": "The Tree Nursery",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003C.quest_desc": [
    "Another multiblock, and a wider one: the core, a Water Tank beside it, and two Solar Panels across the top. The spreader already took a tank and a panel, so budget a second tank and two more panels before you start this.",
    "",
    "Water, Fertilizer and a seedling in. Pick a species on its screen; one sapling comes out after a long cook. A pipe can keep the water topped up, but fertilizer, seedlings and the sapling itself are hand-only, and pulling an input mid-cook drops the progress back to nothing.",
    "",
    "It is also the only source of saplings there is. Nothing drops one, including a tree you cut down yourself.",
    "",
    "Grow oak at some point. Apples come off oak and dark oak leaves and from nowhere else in this world.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003D.title": "Trees Hold It",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003D.quest_desc": [
    "Plant the sapling on grass and leave it room to grow.",
    "",
    "Ground near logs and leaves stops reverting. Nothing else you have holds permanently: grass stays contested and cover only absorbs one hit, so a line of trees along the border is what ends the upkeep.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003E.title": "A Crafting Table",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003E.quest_desc": [
    "The vanilla one. Salvage told you why you could not have it.",
    "",
    "Cut what you grew and build it. A felled tree drops no sapling, so the next tree comes out of the nursery the same way this one did.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003F.title": "Herbivore Bait",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E00003F.quest_desc": [
    "Nothing spawns out here. Any animal in this world is one you put here.",
    "",
    "This one takes an apple and two wheat, so it needs both halves of the chapter: oak for the apple, and a planted seedling that came up wheat for the rest.",
    "",
    "The seedling is also what the nursery wants. Wheat and trees compete.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000040.title": "Leave It Alone",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000040.quest_desc": [
    "Set it on grass and walk away. It settles only while no player is near, then spawns one animal and is spent.",
    "",
    "Walking back over resets its progress to zero rather than pausing it, so checking on it is the one thing that stops it working.",
    "",
    "In a cluster only one settles at a time; the others hold without losing progress and take their turn as each fires.",
    "",
    "Not on grass, nothing happens.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000041.title": "The Other Two Diets",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000041.quest_desc": [
    "Carnivore bait brings cats, ocelots, foxes and armadillos. Omnivore brings chickens, pigs and parrots.",
    "",
    "Carnivore takes two apples and raw meat, and the only meat here walks, so grazers come first. Omnivore is one of each of the other two put together, which makes it three apples and everything that went into both.",
  ],
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000042.title": "A Breeding Pair",
  "quest.7A55E0BA6E000042.quest_desc": [
    "Two of the same bait make the rich version, and it puts down an adult and its young instead of one animal.",
    "",
    "A single animal is a dead end. From a pair, ordinary breeding takes over and the herd keeps itself going without you.",
  ],
}
